+trace and error marks, debug input, JDOR.
+
+### Drawing: `ADDRESS JDOR`
+
+The browser build has no processes, but it has a drawing command environment:
+JDOR ("Java Drawing for ooRexx", Rony G. Flatscher), the command handler of
+BSF4ooRexx850 that turns Java2D into commands, ported to the HTML canvas.
+
+```rexx
+address jdor
+newImage 300 200; color red; moveTo 10 10; fillRect 100 50; winShow
+::requires "jdor.cls"               -- set up the JDOR environment
+```
+
+* Requiring `jdor.cls` sets up the JDOR environment (an image and its
+  window) for the whole interpreter instance; `address jdor` selects it, in
+  each routine, as for any environment.  `call addJdorHandler "NAME"` sets
+  up another one (its own image and window), or gives JDOR a fresh one.
+* The commands, aliases, results (RC), canonical output (`ADDRESS ... WITH
+  OUTPUT`), command input (`WITH INPUT`), error/failure conditions and return
+  codes follow the Java handler (`JavaDrawingHandler.java`, 100.20230718);
+  JDOR's documentation (`jdor_doc.html` in BSF4ooRexx) applies.  Objects
+  that commands return (colors, fonts, images, shapes...) are `JdorObject`s
+  that say what they are, not Java objects: `a JDOR Image (#99)`, `toString`
+  `JDOR Image #99: 500x500, type 2 (ARGB), an OffscreenCanvas`, `kind`
+  `Image`; getters like `rc~width` work, and they can be passed back by
+  variable name, also to another handler.  Where the Java handler throws a
+  Java exception, the ERROR condition's description reads `JDOR (web): ...`.
+* Programs written for BSF4ooRexx also run unchanged: `web/BSF.CLS` (also
+  `bsf.cls`; not the Java bridge, there is no Java here) provides
+  `.bsf~new("org.oorexx.handlers.jdor.JavaDrawingHandler")`,
+  `bsf.importClass` of it, `BsfCommandHandler "add"`, `bsf.createJavaArrayOf`,
+  a few `.java.lang.System~getProperty` values and `pp()`.
+* Implementation: `web-jdor.cpp` is the package `jdor` (routines
+  `JdorNewHandler`, `JdorAddEnvironment`, `JdorSetup`; a redirecting command
+  handler added at run time with `AddCommandEnvironment`), found by
+  `PackageManager` through a weak hook, `orx_wasm_extra_packages()`, that
+  only this build defines.  Each command is passed synchronously
+  (`emscripten_proxy_sync_with_ctx`) to the main runtime thread, the worker
+  that hosts the run and never blocks: `web-jdor.js` (a `--pre-js`) draws on
+  `OffscreenCanvas`es there, possibly finishing later (decoding and encoding
+  images are asynchronous), and asks the C++ side for Rexx variables it needs
+  (nicknames resolved through variables, `assignRC`, `getState`).  Sleeping
+  happens on the interpreter thread.  At most once per animation frame each
+  visible window's image goes to the page as an `ImageBitmap`
+  (`onJdor` in `ooRexx.js`; the page decides how to show windows).  Areas
+  (constructive area geometry) use polygon-clipping (MIT), loaded on first
+  use.
+* Not available: printing and the clipboard depend on the page
+  (`onJdor` 'print' / 'clipboard'); `clipboardGet`; real system fonts (Java's
+  logical fonts map to CSS families, as on Windows); XOR mode is
+  approximated; text antialiasing cannot be turned off.
 
 ## Known limitations / deliberate non-claims
 
